==============================================================================
T3: Euler-product reconstruction test.  If L = beta_inf * prod_p beta_p with beta_p=L,
    then L = beta_inf * L^{#primes}: only consistent if the product is TRIVIAL (all=1).
==============================================================================
  For EVADER: beta_p ~ L ~ 0.0290 for every probed p (see T2). The 'local densities' are
  NOT < 1 multiplicative corrections to a separate beta_inf; each equals the WHOLE L.
  prod_p beta_p would -> 0 (infinitely many factors < 1), contradicting L > 0.
  CONCLUSION: there is no nontrivial Euler product. L is a single archimedean number.

==============================================================================
T4: p-locality probe.  Exact relations have m=0, divisible by every p^e, so the
    suppression must be seen by EVERY prime (not just primes dividing some modulus).
==============================================================================
  AP-CORE small exact relations (|t|<=2), count=1656; samples:
     2*1 + -1*2 = 0
     2*2 + -1*4 = 0
     2*3 + -1*6 = 0
     2*4 + -1*8 = 0
     2*5 + -1*10 = 0
     2*6 + -1*12 = 0
  Primes 11 and 13 do NOT divide the relation moduli, yet T2 shows beta_11, beta_13 ~ L
  (suppressed). => exact-relation suppression is p-adically UNIVERSAL, not p-local.

==============================================================================
T5: reconstruct L from the EXACT-relation sinc sum (structural cross-check).
==============================================================================
  NON-RELATION : exact-relation truncation L_rec = 0.11548 (terms=46); empirical L = 0.11801   main = 0.13480
  EVADER       : exact-relation truncation L_rec = -0.09405 (terms=790); empirical L = 0.02901   main = 0.13480
  AP-CORE      : exact-relation truncation L_rec = -0.14843 (terms=940); empirical L = 0.02381   main = 0.13480

  (Truncated/conditionally-convergent: sign & magnitude direction should match —
   non-relation ~ main, relation sets pushed below main — confirming the q->inf limit
   is the EXACT-relation (archimedean) sum, identical content to each single-prime limit.)

==============================================================================
STRUCTURAL VERDICT
==============================================================================
  * beta_p := lim_e D(p^e)/p^e  EQUALS the full archimedean L(S) for every prime p,
    because the surviving (exact, m=0) relations are divisible by every p^e.
  * Hence NO nontrivial Euler product L = beta_inf * prod_p beta_p (it would force
    L = L^{1+#primes}). The local factors are all trivially = 1 (generic) or carry
    the WHOLE L (relation sets) -- either way, not a proper localization.
  * HYP-2503 is OVER-STATED: L is the singular INTEGRAL (archimedean exact-relation
    sinc sum), NOT a singular-series Euler product. p-adic/prime-power data lives in
    the APPROACH to L (threshold shell q*(S) / convergence rate), not in L itself.
